WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.786
Structured data follows a stable arrangement
Relational databases

00:00:05.812 --> 00:00:09.970
are a classic example because each row follows a
known set of columns and types

00:00:11.827 --> 00:00:17.847
CSV and Parquet files can also contain structured
data The benefit

00:00:17.861 --> 00:00:24.571
is predictability We can validate and query fields
consistently But

00:00:24.584 --> 00:00:30.442
structured does not mean correct A structured table
can still contain duplicates missing

00:00:30.468 --> 00:00:34.258
values inconsistent categories or impossible
measurements
